## Final Result

Server10 and Server30 were successfully configured with a dedicated 172.10.10.0/24 network using their enp0s9 interfaces.

The VirtualBox Internal Network named intnet provided the Layer 2 connection between the two virtual machines.

Both servers were configured with the appropriate IP addresses and verified routes.

The initial connectivity failure was investigated systematically rather than assuming that /etc/hosts was the cause.

ARP was tested directly with arping and network traffic was observed using tcpdump.

After troubleshooting the network at the interface, IP, routing, and Layer 2 levels, communication between Server10 and Server30 was successfully established.

The lab demonstrated that hostname resolution and network connectivity are separate concepts and reinforced the importance of troubleshooting Linux networking one layer at a time.